      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The settlers found this confusing and petitioned the railroad to move its station to the present site of Grove City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.grovecitymn.gov/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early Grove City boasted four grocery stores, two hardware shops, four filling stations, and a barrel factory, among other businesses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.grovecitymn.gov/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office called Grove City has been in operation since 1879, having moved from north of the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grove_City%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The city sits in the watershed of Grove Creek, which flows northeast to join the Middle Fork of the Crow River near Manannah.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grove_City%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
